### API Key Configuration

Set keys via environment variables or the EnvHaven sidebar:

```bash
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...   # Claude Code, OpenCode, Pi, OpenClaw, Hermes, Goose
export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...          # OpenCode, Pi, OpenClaw, Hermes, Goose, Qwen
export GEMINI_API_KEY=...             # OpenCode, Pi, OpenClaw, Hermes, Antigravity
export GOOGLE_API_KEY=...             # OpenCode, OpenClaw, Hermes (alternative)
export MISTRAL_API_KEY=...            # Mistral Vibe
export AMP_API_KEY=...                # Amp
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...         # Hermes (OpenRouter)
export FACTORY_API_KEY=...            # Factory/Droid
export KIRO_API_KEY=...               # Kiro (paid plans)
export XAI_API_KEY=xai-...            # Grok Build
export META_API_KEY=...               # Muse Code
export AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=vck_...     # fx (Vercel AI Gateway)
```

Use the EnvHaven Variables or Launch pane for write-only persistence in
`~/.config/envhaven/environment`. Fresh bash and zsh sessions source that store. You can still add
manual exports to `~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`; EnvHaven detects them but never edits or removes them.
`CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN` is process-owned: set or remove it in the workspace configuration, then restart the workspace.

### Auto-Approve Mode

All tools run with maximum permissions by default. The container IS the sandbox; permission prompts inside it add friction with no security value.

| Tool | Mechanism | To Re-enable Prompts |
|------|-----------|---------------------|
| Claude Code | `~/.claude/settings.json` | Remove `defaultMode` from settings |
| OpenCode | `OPENCODE_PERMISSION` env var | `unset OPENCODE_PERMISSION` |
| fx | `FX_PERMISSION_MODE` env var | `export FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask` (unsetting gives `auto`, which bills a reviewer call instead of asking) |
| Codex | `~/.codex/config.toml` | Remove or edit config file |
| Antigravity CLI | Executable launcher (`--dangerously-skip-permissions`) | `/opt/envhaven/bin/agy` |
| Grok Build | Executable launcher (`--always-approve`) | `/opt/envhaven/bin/grok` |
| Kimi Code CLI | Executable launcher (`--auto`) | `/opt/envhaven/bin/kimi` |
| Muse Code | Bare executable launch (`--disable-approval`, sandbox retained) | `muse --approval-mode on-request` |

Other tools (Goose, Amp, Kiro, etc.) either have no permission system or auto-approve by default.

